# Project: ncaa-quant — NCAA football prediction system

## Authority
docs/DESIGN.md is the specification. Follow it. If a request conflicts with it,
say so and stop rather than guessing. If the spec is genuinely silent on a
detail, make the smallest reasonable choice and record it in docs/adr/.

## Working agreement — applies to every task
- Implement ONLY the module(s) named in the current task. Never edit unrelated
  files. If a task seems to require touching something outside its scope, stop
  and explain instead of doing it.
- Every task ends with: `make test` passing, new code covered by tests,
  docs updated, and an entry appended to docs/notes/<task-number>.md describing
  what was built, decisions made, and anything the spec left ambiguous.
- Do not write speculative code for future tasks. No TODO stubs for later
  subsystems unless the task asks for a stub.

## Non-negotiable engineering rules
- Python 3.11+. ruff + mypy (strict on src/). pandera schemas at every
  DataFrame boundary. All timestamps UTC.
- POINT-IN-TIME CORRECTNESS is the cardinal rule: no function may read data
  whose event_time is later than the as_of timestamp it was called with.
  Never join on game_id without a time bound.
- No random K-fold cross-validation anywhere, ever. Time-ordered splits only.
- All randomness seeded through utils/seeding.py and logged.
- Secrets via pydantic-settings + .env. Never commit .env or hardcode keys.

## Style
- Prefer boring, explicit, testable code over cleverness.
- Type-annotate everything public. Docstrings state units and time semantics.
- Ask before adding a dependency not already in pyproject.toml.

## Environment
- Phase 1 (tasks 1-24) runs NATIVELY with uv. Do not run, start, build, or invoke
  docker or docker-compose.
- MLflow and Prefect run as local processes (`mlflow server`, `prefect server start`).
- Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml exist in the repo as deferred artifacts for a
  possible later containerization phase. Keep them in sync with pyproject.toml when
  dependencies change, but never execute them.
- If containerization becomes in-scope, it will be assigned as its own explicit task.